the parents of the 19 year old Penn  State student who died at a fraternity  house are channeling their grief into a  call for action  Timothy Piazza died in February after an  alleged hazing ritual at the Beta Theta  Pi frat house a grand jury report  details how surveillance cameras inside  captured the events leading to his death  18 fraternity members face charges they  are expected to appear in court later  this week  Jericka Duncan spoke with the Piazza  family and Timothy's girlfriend Rika  good morning good morning Nora Timothy  Piazza's family has not seen the video  that according to the grand jury report  shows fraternity members carrying  Piazza's limp body upstairs smacking him  in the face and pouring liquid on him as  he goes in and out of consciousness for  hours this wasn't boys being boys this  was murder of our son they tortured him  for 12 hours they let him suffer for 12  hours he died a slow and painful death  at the hands of these men of principle  as they call it Jim and Evelyn Piazza  their son Mike and Timothy Piazza's  girlfriend Kaitlyn Tim Polsky are  struggling to make sense of how Timothy  died to hit him and slap him and  brutalize him they should not have been  trying to get a response they should  have been trying to get him help how do  you pour liquid on someone slap them in  the face and hit them after you just  watched them fall and they were  unconscious according to this grand jury  report Beta Theta Pi pledges were forced  to consume heavy amounts of alcohol in a  short amount of time as part of a hazing  ritual within three hours  prosecutors say 19 year-old Piazza fell  down a flight of basement stairs didn't  know that he was laying at the bottom of  the basement steps for any length of  time all by himself  it almost terrible the president of the  university said that Beta Theta Pi will  never return to Penn State University  does that give you some solace No first  of all we told them that had to happen  that's not enough what are the top three  changes you would want to see in the  next six months to a year they need to  eliminate alcohol provided to minors  they need to come down very hard in any  situations where there's hazing and I  think fraternities and sororities maybe  need an adult chaperone  all the time 18 members of Beta Theta Pi  have been charged in connection to  Piazza's death 8 face felony charges  that could result in up to 20 years in  prison I have a lifetime of absence for  my son I would be good with 20 years  what would you say to those students as  they're entering colleges they're  thinking about joining a fraternity or  sorority if anybody tries to make you do  something that's the illegal don't do it  walk away walk away you don't want to be  brothers with those guys do you wish you  would have had that conversation with  your son  we did have some of those conversations  I think the alcohol came fast and  furious and he didn't know you know I  just think it just got away you got  carried away what do you want people to  remember about Timothy about your son  about your brother about your boyfriend  he could always put a smile on  everyone's face he's such a good heart  kind funny he was just an awesome  individual and were a little worse off  as a world without a minute the  fraternity's national organization  disbanded the chapter saying it does not  tolerate hazing or alcohol abuse in any  form that's a sentiment echoed by the  university president since the release  of the grand jury report the university  launched its own investigation the  president of the university says that  could very well lead to expulsion I mean  this family said this isn't just their  son  this was everyone's son because they  feel this could have happened I know I  look at that picture and I think anybody  with a child can relate to that and as  painful as it is  listen it's painful to Rika just to  watch them I can't imagine what it's  like for them to have the feelings that  they have but I'm so glad that they're  speaking out because this is such a  stupid stupid thing yeah enough  happening that their son is dead to me  any facts in dispute about this you know  the defense has not really come out we  heard from some of the attorneys  representing the 18 that have been  charged but they're still you know a lot  to be seen the the preliminary hearing  scheduled for this week we might see  some of that surveillance video that was  in that house and if not for that  surveillance video we probably wouldn't  even be here talking about it I know you  spoke with him for a long time what did  you find out about the outpouring of  support they've received the the mother  and father sat down with me and showed  me numerous cards hundreds of cards that  they received from around the world and  really letting them know that they want  these parents to be an agent of change  they want to make sure that students  recognize the severity involved because  you know we've all been there and like  their parents said this really could  have been anyone's anyone's child it  didn't have to happen nobody called 911  it's it's so sad but I'm very glad you  did that story  thanks I read to the family for speaking  to us
 

